sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-second-assessor-audit-petroff-stromatolite-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — MorphoEval overall 34.0/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass. The script reproduces one scalar relation from Petroff et al. (2010), ell = alpha*sqrt(D*tau), plots it against tau with two script-chosen alpha values, draws a hexagonal lattice of harvest disks at ell(tau=12 h) ~ 0.66 cm, and prints a verbal 'reading the fossil' panel. The lower half of the figure and the GIF are not Petroff's model: they integrate a Lagrangian front advanced by v*z_hat + lambda*n_hat (attributed in the code to Batchelor et al. 2004), multiplied by an ad hoc crest-weighting w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2, with Laplacian smoothing, a pinned base, and a triangular seed. Petroff et al.'s actual shape argument is nutrient-flux limited (quasi-steady diffusion field around neighbouring cones, mat growth set by local diffusive flux), and the paper's evidence is measured cone-spacing distributions from modern Yellowstone mats, laboratory cultures, and Proterozoic/Archean fossils; none of those data or that model appear here. Overall 34.0/100 (faithfulness 27.5, reproducibility 49.1; model-implementation 38.3/100, biological-validation 19.4/100, applicable-only overall 34.0/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 30, Morphological realism / specimen match 22, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 15, Source and data traceability 45, Code-to-model traceability 35, Reproducibility package 62. Output judged: petroff_stromatolite_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py at 5564750, image/png, 328721 B, 1736×1244 px, artifact_sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01 (sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01), spec_fingerprint 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f; artifact_sha256: 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite> ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:136-137 — Release the pinned basal footprint so beta < 1 produces a convex domal stromatolite rather than a vertical-walled trapezoid.",
            "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:193,207,238-239 — Make tau = 12 h (ell = 0.66 cm) and the '~20 h rhythmic metabolism' text panel consistent, and vendor measured modern/lab/fossil cone-spacing distributions and a Conophyton thin-section outline in datasets/petroff/.",
            "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:86-163 — Solve nabla^2 c = 0 around a periodic array of absorbing mats and grow the surface at a rate proportional to local diffusive flux dc/dn, rather than substituting a modified Batchelor front with ad-hoc w_photic (L126-130)." ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.34"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite> rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace faithfully reproduces Photosynthetic microbial mats and conical stromatolites (Conophyton / Yellowstone modern mats) morphology" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor subagent e65a3d81-92b5-4bb2-941f-4566032cb3cd, blinded second assessor)" .
}

